; expect 41
; Renaming consults the rename table BEFORE the for-stack whatever the
; nesting: a `syntax/for` binding pushed inside a template binder of
; the same spelling loses. Here the template `let` binds `g` and an
; argument-position `syntax/for` in its body iterates `g` over the
; struct's fields; each for-body `g` resolves to the `let`'s 41, not
; to the iteration's field name, so the rebuilt point is (41, 41) and
; the answer is 41. Scope resolution would take the innermost binder
; of either kind - the iteration - which is why this program is the
; positive control for `scripts/check-scope-equiv.sh`: under
; AXIOM_VERIFY_SCOPES=1 it must emit AX3075, and without it must
; check clean and answer 41. Whether ren-first or innermost is the
; rule the full scope-sets migration keeps is MAC-HYG-9's open
; question; this fixture pins today's answer either way.
(struct Point
  (x : Int)
  (y : Int))

(macro (probe S) (let ((g 41))
  (S (syntax/for (g (syntax/fields S)) g))))

(:: main Int)
(fn (main)
  (let ((p (probe Point)))
    p.x))
